# Database
# DATABASE_URL is the POOLED connection (Supabase pgbouncer) used by the
# application at runtime. DIRECT_URL is the DIRECT connection used only by
# Prisma CLI operations (migrate/generate) - see the `directUrl` field in
# prisma/schema.prisma. Both are required: a serverless deployment must not
# run migrations through the pooler.
DATABASE_URL=""
DIRECT_URL=""

# Razorpay Test Mode — fill these in once you have created a Razorpay account
# and generated Test Mode keys. Never commit real values (Section 28).
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=""
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=""
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# This deployment uses the single-Razorpay-account architecture (Phase 25
# payment-ingestion merchant-resolution audit): the id of the ONE Merchant
# row (see prisma/schema.prisma) that the account above belongs to. Required
# before any new-Payment creation can be wired up - a webhook can never
# derive Merchant identity from its own payload (see
# apps/web/src/lib/webhooks/merchantResolution.ts). Left unset here on
# purpose; resolveConfiguredMerchant() fails closed until an operator sets a
# real value.
RAZORPAY_MERCHANT_ID=""
